From: vyos-ls1046a-build CI <ci@local>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dpaa1: true zero-copy RX recovery, reprogram/redirect, classify, register (T-M3-3)

Consolidates 0103a (recover-swring) + 0103b (reprogram-redirect) + 0103c
(classify-before-bpid-guard) + 0103e (bpf-net-ctx-fix) + 0103f
(rxhook-before-bpidpool) + 0103g (register-zc-rxq) into one patch, verified
byte-identical against CI checkpoints 032990f2c279..8b8d469f4991
(patch-series-cleanup run 34556757795). (No 0103d ever existed -- gap is
pre-existing, not introduced by this squash.)
Touches: af_xdp_pool_main.c, dpaa_eth.{c,h}, dpaa_ethtool.c.

Signed-off-by: vyos-ls1046a-build CI <ci@local>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_eth.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_eth.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_eth.c
@@ -2509,7 +2509,7 @@
 	if (np->xdp_act & XDP_REDIRECT)
 		xdp_do_flush();
 
-	if (cleaned < budget) {
+if (cleaned < budget) {
 		napi_complete_done(napi, cleaned);
 
 		/* Phase 3a: give the flavor module a chance to arm the
@@ -2518,41 +2518,49 @@
 		 * a single NULL deref under RCU, no behaviour change.
 		 * Spec sec 5.4 RX path step 5.
 		 */
-rcu_read_lock();
-ops = rcu_dereference(priv->qmgmt_ops);
-if (ops && ops->xsk_set_rx_need_wakeup)
-ops->xsk_set_rx_need_wakeup(priv, np);
-
-/* M3-3 step 4 (patch 0084): NAPI-hooked BMan refill from the
- * XSK fill ring. Reuses the local `ops` (no second
- * rcu_dereference), folded into the same RCU read-section as
- * xsk_set_rx_need_wakeup. With no XSK pool bound the callback
- * walks zero bound qbands and returns immediately. Spec sec
- * 6.1.3.
- */
-if (ops && ops->napi_refill)
-ops->napi_refill(priv);
-
-/* M3-3 step 5 (patch 0085): NAPI-hooked TX ZC submission and
- * tx-need-wakeup arming. Same RCU read-section, reuses the
- * local `ops`. napi_tx_zc drains the XSK Tx ring into the
- * DPAA1 egress FQs (xsk_tx_peek_release_desc_batch ->
- * qman_enqueue) honouring the software xsk_tx_inflight budget.
- * xsk_set_tx_need_wakeup arms tx-need-wakeup when the budget
- * is exhausted OR the Tx ring drained. Spec sec 6.1.4.
- */
-if (ops && ops->napi_tx_zc)
-ops->napi_tx_zc(priv);
-if (ops && ops->xsk_set_tx_need_wakeup)
-ops->xsk_set_tx_need_wakeup(priv, np);
+	rcu_read_lock();
+	ops = rcu_dereference(priv->qmgmt_ops);
+	if (ops && ops->xsk_set_rx_need_wakeup)
+	ops->xsk_set_rx_need_wakeup(priv, np);
+
+	/* M3-3 step 5 (patch 0085): NAPI-hooked TX ZC submission and
+	 * tx-need-wakeup arming. Same RCU read-section, reuses the
+	 * local `ops`. napi_tx_zc drains the XSK Tx ring into the
+	 * DPAA1 egress FQs (xsk_tx_peek_release_desc_batch ->
+	 * qman_enqueue) honouring the software xsk_tx_inflight budget.
+	 * xsk_set_tx_need_wakeup arms tx-need-wakeup when the budget
+	 * is exhausted OR the Tx ring drained. Spec sec 6.1.4.
+	 */
+	if (ops && ops->napi_tx_zc)
+	ops->napi_tx_zc(priv);
+	if (ops && ops->xsk_set_tx_need_wakeup)
+	ops->xsk_set_tx_need_wakeup(priv, np);
 
-rcu_read_unlock();
+	rcu_read_unlock();
 
 		qman_p_irqsource_add(np->p, QM_PIRQ_DQRI);
 	} else if (np->down) {
 		qman_p_irqsource_add(np->p, QM_PIRQ_DQRI);
 	}
 
+	/* M3-3 step 4 (patch 0084) / step 7 sub-increment 5 (0103c):
+	 * NAPI-hooked BMan refill from the XSK fill ring.  Runs on
+	 * EVERY poll completion (not just the idle tail), because
+	 * sustained ingress traffic keeps cleaned == budget and the
+	 * idle-tail block above would never execute the refill.
+	 * Without this unconditional refill, the reprogrammed FMan RX
+	 * port drops all XSK-BPID frames at hardware level (BMan pool
+	 * stays empty from the bind-time seed short), and the oracles
+	 * (xsk_zc_eligible / xsk_zc_rx_redirect) stay pinned at 0
+	 * despite successful attach and NAPI wakeup.  Same
+	 * rcu_read_lock() contract; second dereference is cheap.
+	 */
+	rcu_read_lock();
+	ops = rcu_dereference(priv->qmgmt_ops);
+	if (ops && ops->napi_refill)
+		ops->napi_refill(priv);
+	rcu_read_unlock();
+
 	return cleaned;
 }
 
@@ -2842,6 +2850,28 @@
 	fd_format = qm_fd_get_format(fd);
 	net_dev = dpaa_fq->net_dev;
 	priv = netdev_priv(net_dev);
+	/* M3-3 step 7 sub-increment 4b fix (patch 0103f): true-ZC RX consume
+	 * MUST run BEFORE dpaa_bpid2pool(). The attached XSK BMan pool
+	 * (bpid=5) is not in dpaa_bp_array[] -- it is not a kernel page
+	 * pool -- so dpaa_bpid2pool(5) returns NULL and drops the FD.
+	 * This hook recognises the XSK bpid, Recovers the xdp_buff
+	 * from the 0103a reverse map, runs the XDP program, and
+	 * xdp_do_redirect()s into the XSKMAP -- consuming the FD without
+	 * ever needing a kernel page-pool lookup. With no flavor module
+	 * loaded (default flavor) ops is NULL and this branch is dead code
+	 * byte-identical to mainline.
+	 */
+	{
+		const struct dpaa_qmgmt_ops *ops;
+
+		rcu_read_lock();
+		ops = rcu_dereference(priv->qmgmt_ops);
+		if (ops && ops->rx_hook && ops->rx_hook(priv, fq, dq)) {
+			rcu_read_unlock();
+			return qman_cb_dqrr_consume;
+		}
+		rcu_read_unlock();
+	}
 	dpaa_bp = dpaa_bpid2pool(dq->fd.bpid);
 	if (!dpaa_bp)
 		return qman_cb_dqrr_consume;
@@ -2901,6 +2931,33 @@
 		rcu_read_unlock();
 	}
 
+	/* M3-3 step 7 sub-increment 4b (patch 0103b): true-ZC RX consume.
+	 * Give the flavor module first crack at the FD. If it returns true,
+	 * the FD was DMA'd by FMan into a dedicated XSK BMan chunk
+	 * (fd->bpid == priv->xsk_bpid[band]); the flavor has Recovered the
+	 * xdp_buff from the 0103a reverse map and xdp_do_redirect()ed it
+	 * into the XSKMAP (or dropped it per the XDP prog). We MUST NOT
+	 * dma_unmap_page() / build_skb() it -- the chunk is XSK-pool-owned,
+	 * not a kernel page-pool page. Consume the FD and return. Strictly
+	 * NAPI-context (rx_default_dqrr runs under qman_p_poll_dqrr). With
+	 * no flavor module loaded (default flavor) ops is NULL and the fast
+	 * path falls through to the unchanged mainline skbuf path verbatim.
+	 * Dormant until the attach-time reprogram-WRITE makes FMan DMA into
+	 * XSK chunks. Spec sec 6.1.7 mechanism 2 (Recover) + sec 6.1.16.
+	 */
+	{
+		const struct dpaa_qmgmt_ops *ops;
+		bool zc_consumed = false;
+
+		rcu_read_lock();
+		ops = rcu_dereference(priv->qmgmt_ops);
+		if (ops && ops->rx_hook)
+			zc_consumed = ops->rx_hook(priv, fq, dq);
+		rcu_read_unlock();
+		if (zc_consumed)
+			return qman_cb_dqrr_consume;
+	}
+
 	/* Trace the Rx fd */
 	trace_dpaa_rx_fd(net_dev, fq, &dq->fd);
 
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_eth.h b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_eth.h
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_eth.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_eth.h
@@ -239,9 +239,67 @@
 	 */
 	struct xsk_buff_pool __rcu *xsk_pool[DPAA1_XSK_MAX_QBANDS];
 	int                         xsk_bpid[DPAA1_XSK_MAX_QBANDS];
+	/* 0103g: dedicated per-band rxq for true-ZC Recovered frames.
+	 * Registered MEM_TYPE_XSK_BUFF_POOL at ZC attach; stamped into
+	 * every pool xdp_buff via xsk_pool_set_rxq_info() so the rx_hook
+	 * needs no per-frame xdp->rxq assignment.  Without it the first
+	 * Recovered frame NULL-derefs in __xsk_map_redirect
+	 * (xsk_rcv_check reads xdp->rxq->dev; xsk_buff_alloc leaves
+	 * xdp.rxq NULL -- drivers own that field).
+	 */
+	struct xdp_rxq_info         xsk_zc_rxq[DPAA1_XSK_MAX_QBANDS];
 	struct bman_pool           *xsk_bpool[DPAA1_XSK_MAX_QBANDS];
 	unsigned int                xsk_max_qbands;
 
+	/* M3-3 step 7 sub-increment 4a (patch 0103a): true-ZC RX Recover
+	 * sw-ring reverse-map -- DORMANT infrastructure with no datapath
+	 * consumer.  The productive Recover redirect (0103b) needs to turn a
+	 * BMan-returned chunk DMA cookie (qm_fd_addr(fd)) back into the
+	 * originating struct xdp_buff *, but kernel 6.18.31 has no
+	 * xsk_buff_recv()/retrieve-by-dma primitive (the spec sec 6.1.15
+	 * prose named an API that does not exist -- see sec 6.1.16).  Mainline
+	 * ZC drivers (i40e/ice/mlx5) keep a per-RX-ring sw array of the
+	 * xsk_buff_alloc() handles indexed by descriptor; DPAA1's FILL ->
+	 * BMan-release path discards the handle after xsk_buff_xdp_get_dma().
+	 * This array restores that mapping: at FILL-release time 0103b will
+	 * record (chunk_dma -> xdp_buff) here; at RX it will look the cookie
+	 * up.  Allocated/seeded/freed in attach/detach (0103a), but NEITHER
+	 * recorded into NOR consulted by the datapath until 0103b flips the
+	 * reprogram WRITE + redirect on -- so the running kernel is
+	 * byte-identical to the 0102 build on every flavor.
+	 *
+	 * Indexed by qband; each entry is a flat array of
+	 * DPAA1_XSK_INITIAL_SEED struct xdp_buff * slots keyed by UMEM chunk
+	 * index, giving O(1) lookup with no hash collisions.
+	 * xsk_chunk_map_len records the slot count actually allocated
+	 * (0 = dormant/unallocated).
+	 */
+struct xdp_buff           **xsk_chunk_map[DPAA1_XSK_MAX_QBANDS];
+u32                         xsk_chunk_map_len[DPAA1_XSK_MAX_QBANDS];
+
+/* 0103b Recover-redirect: dma_addr_t -> head-index lookup.
+ *
+ * The reverse map above is keyed by the XSK pool head-index
+ * (xskb - pool->heads), which is stable for the pool's lifetime and
+ * directly indexes xsk_chunk_map[band][].  At FILL-release time the
+ * head-index is trivially available from the xdp_buff handle; at RX
+ * only the bare chunk DMA cookie (qm_fd_addr(fd)) survives, and
+ * kernel 6.18.31 exposes no dma_addr_t -> xdp_buff inversion.
+ *
+ * xsk_chunk_dma[band] is a sorted array of the per-head DMA cookies
+ * built once at attach (after xsk_pool_dma_map()); the parallel
+ * xsk_chunk_dma_idx[band] holds the matching head-index for each
+ * sorted cookie.  At RX an O(log n) bsearch on xsk_chunk_dma[]
+ * recovers the head-index, which then indexes xsk_chunk_map[].  This
+ * is correct for BOTH aligned-contiguous and fragmented UMEMs (no
+ * subtract+shift contiguity assumption -- spec sec 6.1.8 crash
+ * class).  Allocated/sorted in attach, freed in detach; NULL/0 when
+ * dormant.  xsk_chunk_dma_cnt is the sorted-entry count.
+ */
+dma_addr_t                 *xsk_chunk_dma[DPAA1_XSK_MAX_QBANDS];
+u32                        *xsk_chunk_dma_idx[DPAA1_XSK_MAX_QBANDS];
+u32                         xsk_chunk_dma_cnt[DPAA1_XSK_MAX_QBANDS];
+
 	/* AF_XDP zerocopy ethtool / debugfs counters. Bumped by the
 	 * flavor module's attach/detach/NAPI paths. Phase 2 introduces
 	 * attach/detach/seed/dma/align/headroom/mtu/pamu counters;
@@ -364,6 +422,32 @@
  */
 u64 xsk_zc_rx_recovered;
 
+/* M3-3 step 7 sub-increment 4a (patch 0103a): Recover sw-ring
+ * reverse-map diagnostic.  Bumped by dpaa_xsk_chunk_lookup() when a
+ * chunk DMA cookie is successfully resolved back to its xdp_buff.
+ * DORMANT: the lookup helper is exercised by a one-shot self-test at
+ * attach time (record N, look the same N back, free), but the RX
+ * hot-path does NOT call it until 0103b.  Increments exactly once
+ * per successful attach (the self-test) -- 0 until the first
+ * XDP_ZEROCOPY bind, then a small fixed number, never growing with
+ * traffic until 0103b.  21st xsk_* line.
+ */
+u64 xsk_zc_recover_lookup;
+
+/* M3-3 step 7 sub-increment 4b (patch 0103b): productive true-ZC RX
+ * redirect success counter.  Bumped by af_xdp_pool_rx_hook() each
+ * time a recognised XSK-pool FD is Recovered to its xdp_buff and
+ * xdp_do_redirect()ed into the XSKMAP (the hook then consumes the
+ * FD and the core RX path never builds an skb for it).  Unlike the
+ * dormant 0096 xsk_zc_rx_recovered (which only OBSERVES that the
+ * Recover decision would be taken while the FD still travels the
+ * skbuf path), this counts ACTUAL zero-copy redirects -- it grows
+ * with traffic once the 0103b reprogram-WRITE points the FMan RX
+ * port at the dedicated XSK BMan pool.  0 on default/vpp (no
+ * XDP_ZEROCOPY bind, no reprogram).  22nd xsk_* line.
+ */
+u64 xsk_zc_rx_redirect;
+
 /* M3-3b (patch 0086): FMan PCD capability bitmask snapshot taken
  * at probe via dpaa_fman_get_caps(). 0 on mainline ucode 106 ->
  * all fman_cc_tree_/fman_hm_/fman_pol_ helpers short-circuit
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_ethtool.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_ethtool.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_ethtool.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_ethtool.c
@@ -75,6 +75,8 @@
 "xsk_zc_rx_armed",
 "xsk_fill_guard_block",
 "xsk_zc_rx_recovered",
+"xsk_zc_recover_lookup",
+"xsk_zc_rx_redirect",
 };
 
 /* HW-offload (PCD-cap) counters (M3-3b / patch 0086). Order MUST match
